    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39687" root="نسأ" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَاسِئٌ</span></b> , pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَسَأَةٌ</span> (S) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَاسِئُونَ</span>, (TA,) <i>One
whose office it was to perform the act called</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَسِىْء</span>; <i>i. e., the postponing of a month:</i> (S, TA:)
he was also called <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَلَمَّسٌ</span>, pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَلَامِسُ</span>. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَاسِئٌ</span> Anything <i>fat:</i> or <i>beginning to grow fat:</i>
in the K it is said, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كُلُّ نَاسِئٍ سَمِينٌ</span>: in the L,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كلّ سمين ناسئ</span>, which is more proper. (TA.)

